    description: "Found 2026-08-10 while adding Go composite-literal receiver typing.\n\nTHE FIXTURE COULD NOT FAIL. test_go_return_type_registry.py's go_available fixture\nprobed _analyzer.is_grammar_available() inside a bare `except Exception: pytest.skip`.\nNo such method exists -- is_grammar_available is a MODULE FUNCTION in\nhypergumbo_core.analyze.base, not a method on the analyzer object -- so every call\nraised AttributeError, the handler swallowed it, and all three integration tests\nreported \"Go analyzer not available\" on a machine where tree_sitter_go is installed and\nthe 15 unit tests in the same file pass.\n\nThey had never executed. The unit half of WI-kuroj / INV-dihos was covered; the\nend-to-end half was a green tick over a hole.\n\nWHEN THE FIXTURE IS REPAIRED, ALL THREE FAIL:\n  test_chained_method_call_resolves_via_registry\n  test_constructor_return_type_enables_chaining\n  test_tuple_return_with_error_resolves\n\nObserved on `result := e.Query(); result.Rows()`:\n  expected  a calls edge to Result.Rows\n  actual    go:external:0-0:Rows:unresolved\n\nA/B CONFIRMS PRE-EXISTING, NOT INTRODUCED. Reverting go.py to dev (c675fc484f) and\nre-running with the repaired fixture reproduces all three failures identically. The\ncomposite-literal PR neither caused nor fixes them.\n\nTHE REGISTRY IS WIRED, SO THIS IS NOT A PLUMBING GAP. method_return_type_registry is\nbuilt at go.py:4444-4447 and passed to _extract_edges_from_file at go.py:4471; it\nreaches _extract_go_var_types (go.py:2301) and the consumption sites at go.py:1759-1772\nand go.py:2553-2574. Something inside that chain does not fire. Not localized further.\n\nCORROBORATING SMELL, same area: the WI-kuroj fallback block at go.py:1715-1732 carries\n`# pragma: no cover - requires Go tree-sitter grammar` while the grammar IS installed\nand the surrounding code is exercised -- the pragma is excusing itself on the same false\npremise that kept the tests skipped.\n\nDISPOSITION IN THE MEANTIME: the three tests are marked xfail(strict=True) rather than\nleft skipped, so they RUN, fail honestly, and flip the suite red the moment the feature\nstarts working (prompting removal of the marker). The repaired fixture has no exception\nhandler at all -- a skip reachable by a typo is what caused this."  # a062
    fields: {}  # a062
